WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.420 --> 00:00:08.380
The only thing that is constant is change.

00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:12.200
Everything around us is always changing

00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:15.580
We see things moving, the weather keeps changing,

00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:18.220
prices of things are always changing.

00:00:18.220 --> 00:00:20.900
The temperature of the earth keeps rising.

00:00:21.040 --> 00:00:23.340
Our population keeps increasing

00:00:23.340 --> 00:00:26.080
and many more such changes.

00:00:26.320 --> 00:00:28.920
Wouldn't it be amazing if we can predict

00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:31.220
how things are going to change?

00:00:31.480 --> 00:00:33.480
Well in many cases,

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:37.240
Calculus is the branch of mathematics that can do this.

00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:39.100
For example,

00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:43.380
calculus is used for analyzing the motion of objects

00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:45.100
and then to build the models

00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:48.540
to predict the trajectory of things like rockets.

00:00:48.780 --> 00:00:51.840
It can be used to analyze the money coming in and out

00:00:51.880 --> 00:00:52.660
of a business

00:00:53.180 --> 00:00:56.380
and then to build models to maximize its profit.

00:00:56.760 --> 00:00:58.360
Calculus can be referred to

00:00:58.440 --> 00:01:00.980
as the mathematics of change.

00:01:01.240 --> 00:01:03.460
So to develop the skill of predicting

00:01:03.480 --> 00:01:05.440
change in the upcoming set of videos

00:01:05.780 --> 00:01:09.040
we are going to understand the basic concepts of

00:01:09.140 --> 00:01:10.760
Calculus.

00:01:11.080 --> 00:01:14.120
Limits, differentiation and integration

00:01:14.480 --> 00:01:18.800
are the important ideas around which calculus is built.

00:01:19.180 --> 00:01:22.420
First we'll understand these ideas

00:01:22.760 --> 00:01:24.840
in calculus if we mostly study things

00:01:25.040 --> 00:01:27.700
which change according to a pattern.

00:01:28.040 --> 00:01:29.600
These patterns of change

00:01:29.780 --> 00:01:31.640
are mathematically represented by the

00:01:31.640 --> 00:01:33.480
concept of functions

00:01:33.720 --> 00:01:36.140
So the concept of functions is the main

00:01:36.240 --> 00:01:38.300
object of study in calculus.

00:01:38.660 --> 00:01:41.960
And therefore, we will understand it well.

00:01:42.560 --> 00:01:43.400
And finally,

00:01:43.720 --> 00:01:47.260
we will see how to use the ideas of limits, differentiation

00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:50.900
and integration to analyze functions.

00:01:51.200 --> 00:01:53.800
So to see a positive change in your knowledge of

00:01:53.920 --> 00:01:54.940
mathematics,

00:01:55.140 --> 00:01:58.080
watch the upcoming videos to understand the

00:01:58.340 --> 00:01:59.780
basics of calculus.

